  "name": "Maintain a public integration catalog in StudioCMS from GitHub",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "bbbaf67d-5f93-4cc0-b054-0b08df2c0be2",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -704,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 562,
        "height": 756,
        "content": "## Maintain a public integration catalog in StudioCMS from GitHub\n\n### How it works\n\nRuns manually or every day, lists repositories from a configurable GitHub organization, keeps only the chosen repository prefix, and reads each repository's README, package metadata, and latest release. It builds one deterministic StudioCMS page per integration and safely creates, updates, or skips it by exact slug. Archived repositories become drafts; nothing is deleted.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Select GitHub and StudioCMS credentials on the service nodes.\n- Edit **Configure Integration Catalog** for the organization, prefix, folder, slug prefix, and publishing behavior.\n- Keep **previewOnly** enabled for the first run and inspect the final report.\n- Set **previewOnly** to false after the proposed changes look correct.\n- Activate only when the daily schedule is appropriate for the site.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange `githubOwner` and `repositoryPrefix` to reuse this for another integration catalog. Adjust the Markdown in **Build Structured Catalog Page** to match the site's design. The ownership marker prevents overwriting an unrelated hand-built page with the same slug. Missing READMEs, invalid package metadata, and page conflicts are surfaced in the final report instead of silently discarded."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4f0409cd-3269-466d-9c86-8cc3ddfae79a",
      "name": "Section 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -96,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 820,
        "height": 496,
        "content": "## 1. Start and validate\n\nRun manually while configuring or let the daily schedule start the workflow after activation. Central settings make the organization, repository prefix, folder, publishing mode, and safe preview behavior easy to reuse."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1f31aeb6-9b65-434e-a520-d9553cd6ae84",
      "name": "Section 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        784,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1492,
        "height": 784,
        "content": "## 2. Resolve the StudioCMS destination\n\nFind the exact catalog folder, reject ambiguous duplicates, and create it only during a live run. Preview mode reports that the folder would be created. Existing pages are loaded once for deterministic comparison."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "0aab2da7-fbba-4529-a129-466993bc095c",
      "name": "Section 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2320,
        144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 480,
        "content": "## 3. Select integration repositories\n\nList the GitHub organization, filter early by the configured prefix and fork policy, de-duplicate, sort, cap the workload, and process repositories sequentially to respect API limits."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "35adcb84-1b8a-4094-a368-3851147e76be",
      "name": "Section 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3520,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 2100,
        "height": 448,
        "content": "## 4. Build an evidence-based catalog page\n\nRead README.md and package.json from the repository's default branch, retrieve the latest GitHub release, then build consistent Markdown containing version, compatibility, supported operations, install command, links, and release notes. Missing optional source data becomes a warning."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "05961ee0-9a66-43d1-85cb-ca6be99bd665",
      "name": "Section 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        5664,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1290,
        "height": 1400,
        "content": "## 5. Upsert safely and report\n\nCompare the generated source digest and exact slug. Create or update only pages owned by this workflow, skip unchanged pages, keep archived integrations as drafts, and aggregate preview actions, writes, conflicts, and warnings into a final report."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
